**********Source Check**********

The claim 'The two user studies validated Grab-n-Go's in a certain state.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The text explicitly states in the Abstract, "A follow-up study further validated Grab-n-Go’s robustness against 10 more challenging, deformable objects." and in the Introduction, "The two studies validated the system’s robustness and generalizability." </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'A customized deep learning model infers microgestures from something.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The text explicitly states in the abstract, "A deep learning framework processes these complex signals to identify 30 distinct microgestures," and in the Figure 1 caption, "echo profiles can be created to infer the microgestures using a customized deep learning model." Section 4.3 further elaborates, "To recognize microgestures, we developed a customized deep-learning pipeline." These statements confirm that a customized deep learning model infers microgestures from complex signals or echo profiles. </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'Grab-n-Go achieved an average recognition accuracy of 92.0% in an initial user study.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The abstract and the introduction explicitly state that "In a user study with 10 participants and 25 everyday objects, Grab-n-Go achieved an average recognition accuracy of 92.0%." This study is also referred to as the initial study, followed by a "follow-up study" or "another study". </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'The two user studies validated Grab-n-Go's robustness.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The content explicitly states under the "Contributions" section: "We conducted a user study with 10 participants performing 30 microgestures across 5 distinct grasping poses and 25 different objects. This was followed by another study with 8 participants using 10 deformable objects. The two studies validated the system’s robustness and generalizability." Additionally, in the abstract, it mentions: "A follow-up study further validated Grab-n-Go’s robustness against 10 more challenging, deformable objects." </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'A customized deep learning model infers microgestures from echo profiles.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The claim is explicitly mentioned in the Figure 1 caption: "echo profiles can be created to infer the microgestures using a customized deep learning model." The abstract also states, "A deep learning framework processes these complex signals to identify 30 distinct microgestures," and the description of Figure 1 clarifies that "These profiles are fed into a deep learning model. The model looks at the patterns in the echoes to predict...the gesture being made." </accept>

