*   In the same paper , they showed that this stretch-lightness tradeoff is existentially tight (up to a log()−1 factor): For any 2≤d=O(1), there exists an nn-point set in Rd (the aforementioned set of evenly spaced points on the dd-dimensional sphere), for which any (1+)-spanner has something.

